 ],
 "position_rule_in_words": "Per account, take its rows inside the window in date order and call a row OK or non-OK by its status (the reader's own test, holdings_gold.py:246). The account has an excluded day when the reader returns a figure and days_excluded is 1 or more. last_day_involved: the account's LAST row in the window is non-OK (whatever else). Otherwise, with its first OK row as the dividing point: first_day_only: every non-OK row comes before the first OK row (a leading run of one or more days, e.g. an account not yet funded); interior_only: every non-OK row lies after the first OK row and before the last row (a day between OK days, chained across); first_and_interior: non-OK rows both before the first OK row and between OK days. The four classes are exclusive and cover the accounts with an excluded day. A refused account (no OK row at all, or an account the reader cannot map) is not placed.",
 "status_values": {
